<title>SWEDEN: Stena ready to take up slack in Channel.</title>
<headline>Stena ready to take up slack in Channel.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stena Line said it was ready to take up any excess demand for cross-Channel traffic after fire in the undersea tunnel hit train services between England and France.</p>
<p>&quot;Ferry traffic over the Channel is going into the low season and we have capacity to absorb traffic which cannot travel via Eurotunnel, Stena Line's information director Mats Kling told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said it was too early to say whether the fire would impact Stena Line's earnings for the year, as it was not clear how long one of the two main tunnels would be closed for repairs.</p>
<p>Stena Lines forecasts a 1996 loss of 450 million crowns. It has five ferries making 26 crossings per day Dover-Calais.</p>
<p>-- Peter Fellman, Stockholm Newsroom 08-700 1007</p>
</text>
